hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1150","Chapter on the purposes for which fay' wealth is disbursed, 1190 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray over a man with a debt. A dead man was brought, and he asked: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he prayed over him. He said: When Allah granted His Messenger conquests, he said: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves a debt, it is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"1151","1191 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: When anything came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would distribute it the same day. He would give a married man two shares and an unmarried man one share. He said: So I was called - and I used to be called before Ammar ibn Yasir - and I was called and he gave me two shares, for I had a family. Then Ammar was called after, and he gave him one share."
"1152","1192 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib informed him that Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib met and said: By Allah, if we sent these two lads - meaning himself and al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas - to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would appoint them over these charities. He mentioned part of the hadith. He said: So we spoke to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to you that you appoint us over these charities. He said: Charity is not fitting for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad; it is but the people's impurities. Call Mahmiyah ibn al-Jaz' for me - he was in charge of tithes - and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith. They both came to him, and he said to Mahmiyah: Marry this lad to your daughter, for al-Fadl; so he married him to her. And he said to Abu Sufyan: Marry this lad to your daughter; so he married him to her. Then he said to Mahmiyah: Pay their bridal gifts from the fifth."
"1153","1193 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam informed us that Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to them, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that when Mu'awiyah came to Medina performing pilgrimage, Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) came to him. Mu'awiyah said to him: Your need, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said to him: My need is the stipend of the freedmen, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when anything came to him, begin with none before them."
